{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"The baseline passes all 16 workloads. I’m now switching to a collision-aware fused design: unique token rows write directly in BF16, only duplicated token IDs use FP32 atomics, and normalization statistics are reduced in a dedicated tiled pass. This preserves scatter semantics without paying for a full 1 GiB FP32 embedding buffer."}}
