{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"agent_message","text":"The new linked-list scatter cut the largest case from ~19 ms to ~1.8 ms, and its math kernels are already near bandwidth limits. The remaining bottleneck is list construction: scalar CAS programs cost ~0.77 ms. I’m vectorizing that lock-free insertion with padded per-token dummy slots, which should reduce it to the histogram-scale range."}}
